274: ## Course-level checks
275: 
276: | Check | After unit | Check days | Respond days | What it checks |
277: |---|---|---|---|---|
278: | Year 3 mid-year (week 18, days 35 and 36) | 2 | 1 | 1 | Samples units 1 and 2 in their own year: a written art-detective sheet on an unseen print or collage, two clues to how it was made and the message it sends (VA:Re7.1.3a, VA:Re7.2.3a), and a fresh short task adding two layers of detail and depth to a given invented-creature sketch (VA:Cr1.1.3a). Unit 2's revised work and note (its check day, day 33) are carried unscored; no idea-page task repeats. Respond on day 36. |
279: | Year 3 year-end (week 26, days 51 and 52) | 3 | 1 | 1 | Samples units 1 to 3: a written response on an unseen work, how its media build subject and mood and what it means (VA:Re8.1.3a), the same work judged with a new three-line checklist (VA:Re9.1.3a), and a given drawing revised by one added detail with a one-line reason (VA:Cr3.1.3a, unit 2). Unit 3's product records (days 48 and 49) are carried unscored. Unit 4 is assessed by its own showing. Respond on day 52. |
