e map or sketch set: places or objects that matter named, described and drawn; VA:Cn10.1.5a, a guide look-for on the made work: at least four art and design words used as labels, and one thing never noticed before shown; VA:Re8.1.5a, a written item: the ideas and mood of an unseen work from its form, structure, setting card, subject, visual elements and media; VA:Re9.1.5a, a written item: two unseen works from different styles or cultures, each with a setting card, and one way the standards used to judge each differ. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: designing for named users (grade 6). Tools: the "made for" card, a symmetry fold card, setting cards, Curio Class's own. Free path: pencils, scrap paper, a folded paper square. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | After unit 10 because labeling in art and design words and comparing standards use the statement's art words; before unit 12 because a curator's argument and an exhibit's evidence need standards and settings already compared | Candidate: a fourth work judged by different standards, from Africa or the Americas, described and linked | Places that matter: invited, never required, with a public or invented place marked the same; no home address or route is drawn. Iznik tiles were made for mosques, palaces and tombs: the unit tells the setting, studies the pattern by looking, and the sensitivity agent reads the Met's page first. Hazards and controls: pencils and colored pencils only; the walk to look for pattern and symmetry stays on school grounds. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
